[
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-01",
    "role": "opening",
    "config": {
      "text": "A lion's body.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "A woman's face.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Wings folded on her back.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "She watches over the city of Thebes, and asks its people a riddle.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Those who cannot answer, she destroys.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-06",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "This is the Sphinx of Greek legend.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-07",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Yet the most famous sphinx in the world, the great one in Egypt, never asked anyone a riddle.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P01-08",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "It is not even a woman.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P02-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In this episode, we look at two very different sphinxes, the guardian of Egypt and the riddler of Greece, and at how one name came to cover them both.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Great Sphinx of Giza was carved from the living rock of the desert, about four and a half thousand years ago.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Many scholars link it to King Khafre, whose pyramid rises behind it.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "mˈɛni skˈɑːlɚz lˈɪŋk ɪt tə kˈɪŋ kˈæfɹeɪ , hˌuːz pˈɪɹɐmˌɪd ɹˈaɪzᵻz bᵻhˈaɪnd ɪt."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Its face wears the royal headcloth of a pharaoh.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P03-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Its body is a lion at rest.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In Egypt, the lion stood for power, and the sphinx joined that power to the face of the king.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Sphinxes lined the roads to temples and kept watch over sacred places.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Most of them show a king.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P04-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Hatshepsut, a woman who ruled as pharaoh, appears here as a sphinx too, with the royal headcloth and the ceremonial beard of a king.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "hætʃˈɛpsuːt , ɐ wˈʊmən hˌuː ɹˈuːld æz fˈɛɹoʊ, ɐpˈɪɹz hˈɪɹ æz ɐ sfˈɪŋks tˈuː, wɪððə ɹˈɔɪəl hˈɛdklɔθ ænd ðə sˌɛɹᵻmˈoʊnɪəl bˈɪɹd əvə kˈɪŋ."
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "We do not know what the builders of Giza called their sphinx.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "More than a thousand years later, Egyptians worshipped it as a god, Horemakhet, \"Horus in the Horizon.\" Between its paws stands a stone set up by King Thutmose the Fourth.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "mˈɔːɹ ðˌænə θˈaʊzənd jˈɪɹz lˈeɪɾɚ, ɪdʒˈɪpʃənz wˈɜːʃɪpt ɪɾ æz ɐ ɡˈɑːd, hɔːɹɛmˈɑːkɛt , \"hˈɔːɹəs ɪnðə hɚɹˈaɪzən.\" bᵻtwˌiːn ɪts pˈɔːz stˈændz ɐ stˈoʊn sˈɛt ˌʌp baɪ kˈɪŋ θuːtmˈoʊsə ðə fˈɔːɹθ."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "It tells how, as a young prince, he rested in the shadow of the great god.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P05-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In a dream, the god promised him the kingdom, and said that the sand of the desert had reached him.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In these Egyptian statues and stones, there is no riddle.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The sphinx here does not test travelers.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P06-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "It guards kings and gods.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In Greece, the sphinx was something else.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The poet Hesiod, writing around 700 BC, lists her among a family of monsters, and calls her the destroyer of the people of Thebes.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "ðə pˈoʊɪt hˈiːsiːɑːd , ɹˈaɪɾɪŋ ɚɹˈaʊnd sˈɛvənhˈʌndɹɪd bˌiːsˈiː, lˈɪsts hɜːɹ ɐmˌʌŋ ɐ fˈæmɪli ʌv mˈɔnstɚz, ænd kˈɔːlz hɜː ðə dᵻstɹˈɔɪɚɹ ʌvðə pˈiːpəl ʌv θˈiːbz."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P07-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In this passage, he says nothing about a riddle.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Greek artists usually gave the sphinx a woman's head, a lion's body, and the wings of a bird.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Often they set her on top of a grave marker, watching over the dead.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P08-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "This sphinx once crowned a grave in Attica, around 530 BC.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Where the name came from is uncertain.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Some link it to a Greek word meaning \"to squeeze\" or \"to bind.\" Others have looked for an Egyptian origin.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P09-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "No one knows for sure.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The riddle belongs to the stories of Thebes, told on the stage in Athens in the four hundreds BC.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In Sophocles' play Oedipus the King, the people remember \"the riddling Sphinx,\" and Oedipus is the stranger who freed the city from her.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "ˈɪn sˈɑːfoʊkliːz plˈeɪ ˈiːdɪpəs ðə kˈɪŋ, ðə pˈiːpəl ɹᵻmˈɛmbɚ \"ðə ɹˈɪdlɪŋ sfˈɪŋks,\" ænd ˈiːdɪpəs ɪz ðə stɹˈeɪndʒɚ hˌuː fɹˈiːd ðə sˈɪɾi fɹʌm hɜː."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P10-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Painters have returned to this meeting ever since.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But the play never gives the words of the riddle.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "We find them in later writers, such as Athenaeus, and a handbook of myths called the Library.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "wiː fˈaɪnd ðˌɛm ɪn lˈeɪɾɚ ɹˈaɪɾɚz, sˈʌtʃ ɐz æθənˈiːəs , ænd ɐ hˈændbʊk ʌv mˈɪθs kˈɔːld ðə lˈaɪbɹɛɹi."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-03",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "They ask: what has one voice, and becomes four-footed, two-footed, and three-footed?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "The answer is a human being.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "A baby crawls, an adult walks, and the old lean on a staff.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-06",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "In these texts, there is no morning, noon, or evening.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P11-07",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And when the riddle was solved, the Library says, the Sphinx threw herself down.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "So how did one name come to mean both?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "We do not know every step.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "But the Greek name stayed.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "When the historian Herodotus, in the four hundreds BC, described the great statues a king set up at a temple in Sais, in Egypt, he called them androsphinxes, sphinxes with the heads of men.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "wˌɛn ðə hɪstˈɔːɹiən hɪɹˈɑːdəɾəs, ɪnðə fˈɔːɹ hˈʌndɹɪdz bˌiːsˈiː, dᵻskɹˈaɪbd ðə ɡɹˈeɪt stˈætʃuːz ɐ kˈɪŋ sˈɛt ˌʌp æɾə tˈɛmpəl ˈɪn sˈeɪɪs , ɪn ˈiːdʒɪpt, hiː kˈɔːld ðˌɛm ˈændɹəsfˌɪŋksᵻz, sfˈɪŋksᵻz wɪððə hˈɛdz ʌv mˈɛn."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P12-05",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "And we still call the guardian of Giza by the name of a Greek monster.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-01",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Its face carries another story.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-02",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "It is often said that Napoleon's soldiers shot off its nose.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-03",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "Yet drawings by the Danish traveler Frederic Norden, who visited in the seventeen thirties, already show the face without its nose.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12,
      "phonemes": "jˈɛt dɹˈɔːɪŋz baɪ ðə dˈeɪnɪʃ tɹˈævəlɚ fɹˈɛdɹɪk nˈɔːɹdən, hˌuː vˈɪzɪɾᵻd ɪnðə sˈɛvəntˌiːn θˈɜːɾiz, ɔːlɹˌɛdi ʃˈoʊ ðə fˈeɪs wɪðˌaʊt ɪts nˈoʊz."
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P13-04",
    "role": "plain",
    "config": {
      "text": "They were printed long before Napoleon came to Egypt in 1798.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-01",
    "role": "question",
    "config": {
      "text": "So, did the Sphinx ask riddles?",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-02",
    "role": "conclusion",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Greek one did, in the stories of Thebes.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
  },
  {
    "sentence_id": "P14-03",
    "role": "conclusion",
    "config": {
      "text": "The Egyptian one, far older, was a king in the shape of a lion, keeping watch at the edge of the desert.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "speed": 0.82,
      "sentence_pause": 0.3,
      "clause_pause": 0.12
    },
    "gap_after": 0.3
